   "text": {
    "L1": "The poem shows a child who exercises and eats fresh fruit and greens.",
    "L2": "The child gets up at six and says, “I’m always full of beans!”",
    "L3": "That saying does not mean the child ate many beans.",
    "L4": "“Full of beans” means full of energy. Exercise and healthy food help the child feel energetic.",
    "L5": "The action words include stretch, run, jump and skip.",
    "L6": "For daily habits, use the simple present: “I drink milk every morning.”",
    "L7": "Use “at” for a clock time and “in the morning” or “in the evening” for part of a day.",
    "L8": "A fit body and a calm mind help people work hard and help others, making a strong and kind nation."
   },
